http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135851866,imgsize-52508.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bengal CM Suvendu Adhikari accuses TMC of treating only Muslims as minorities]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bengal-cm-suvendu-adhikari-accuses-tmc-of-treating-only-muslims-as-minorities/articleshow/135851530.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135851530.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Suvendu Adhikari visited Gurdwara Bara Sikh Sangat in Burrabazar to meet the Sikh community. During his visit, he expressed gratitude towards the Sikh community and participated in a procession. Adhikari criticized the previous Trinamool Congress government for only recognizing Muslims as minority communities. He stated that Sikhs, Buddhists, and Jains should also be considered religious minorities. Adhikari accused the TMC government of engaging in political appeasement for electoral support.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bengal-cm-suvendu-adhikari-accuses-tmc-of-treating-only-muslims-as-minorities/articleshow/135851530.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bengal-cm-suvendu-adhikari-accuses-tmc-of-treating-only-muslims-as-minorities/articleshow/135851530.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T14:13:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135851567,imgsize-74100.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Air purifier sales surge as pollution turns severe, demand spreads beyond metros]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-purifier-sales-surge-as-pollution-turns-severe-demand-spreads-beyond-metros/articleshow/135850815.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135850815.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In India, the demand for air purifiers has skyrocketed, largely due to deteriorating air quality. Delhi-NCR notably drives this surge, experiencing sales boosts, particularly post-Diwali. Many manufacturers and retailers are reporting sales volumes that have doubled during this festive season. Additionally, the rise of online shopping indicates a changing consumer trend focused on air purification. The troubling Air Quality Index in Delhi further fuels this demand.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-purifier-sales-surge-as-pollution-turns-severe-demand-spreads-beyond-metros/articleshow/135850815.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-purifier-sales-surge-as-pollution-turns-severe-demand-spreads-beyond-metros/articleshow/135850815.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T13:45:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135850815,imgsize-3863390.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Govt will teach 'Dimagi Naxals' a lesson’: BJP chief Nitin Nabin in Chattisgarh]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-will-teach-dimagi-naxals-a-lesson-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-in-chattisgarh/articleshow/135850769.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135850769.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-will-teach-dimagi-naxals-a-lesson-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-in-chattisgarh/articleshow/135850769.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/govt-will-teach-dimagi-naxals-a-lesson-bjp-chief-nitin-nabin-in-chattisgarh/articleshow/135850769.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T13:42:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135850961,imgsize-71108.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Embed quality into every stage': Rajnath Singh calls for stricter checks in defence manufacturing]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/embed-quality-into-every-stage-rajnath-singh-calls-for-stricter-checks-in-defence-manufacturing/articleshow/135850168.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135850168.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/embed-quality-into-every-stage-rajnath-singh-calls-for-stricter-checks-in-defence-manufacturing/articleshow/135850168.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/embed-quality-into-every-stage-rajnath-singh-calls-for-stricter-checks-in-defence-manufacturing/articleshow/135850168.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T13:30:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135850657,imgsize-36346.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Undeclared Emergency under BJP rule': JMM backs Rahul Gandhi's remarks on democracy]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/undeclared-emergency-under-bjp-rule-jmm-backs-rahul-gandhis-remarks-on-democracy/articleshow/135850259.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135850259.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a recent statement, Jharkhand Mukti Morcha spokesperson Manoj Pandey voiced his alignment with Rahul Gandhi's critique of the BJP-led government's actions. He asserted that India is witnessing an unspoken Emergency, compromising democratic principles and citizen rights. Pandey underscored a significant decline in democratic institutions over the last twelve years, hinting at a concerning trend.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/undeclared-emergency-under-bjp-rule-jmm-backs-rahul-gandhis-remarks-on-democracy/articleshow/135850259.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/undeclared-emergency-under-bjp-rule-jmm-backs-rahul-gandhis-remarks-on-democracy/articleshow/135850259.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T13:11:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135850362,imgsize-75590.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Law on our side': Karnataka minister's big remark amid Mekedatu Dam row with Tamil Nadu]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/law-on-our-side-karnataka-ministers-big-remark-amid-mekedatu-dam-row-with-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135850140.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135850140.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Karnataka minister Priyank Kharge said the law supported the state's proposed Mekedatu dam project, stressing that both Karnataka and Tamil Nadu must follow the Supreme Court's directions. The remarks came amid BJP accusations of Congress double standards over opposition to the project in Tamil Nadu. Karnataka maintains its right to build the reservoir to meet Bengaluru's drinking water needs and generate hydroelectric power, while protecting Tamil Nadu's Cauvery water share.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/law-on-our-side-karnataka-ministers-big-remark-amid-mekedatu-dam-row-with-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135850140.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/law-on-our-side-karnataka-ministers-big-remark-amid-mekedatu-dam-row-with-tamil-nadu/articleshow/135850140.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T13:04:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vivek Dubey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135850237,imgsize-90662.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Abandoned tribals to Naxal violence’: PM Modi takes aim at previous govts]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/abandoned-tribals-to-naxal-violence-pm-modi-takes-aim-at-previous-govts/articleshow/135849329.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135849329.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi addressed the Janjatiya Gaurav Diwas programme, emphasizing the impact of Naxal violence on tribal communities. He stated that previous governments neglected tribals and denied them their rights. Modi announced significant funding exceeding Rs 1 lakh crore for tribal area development initiatives. He mentioned the inauguration of 246 projects aimed at improving tribal livelihoods and infrastructure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/abandoned-tribals-to-naxal-violence-pm-modi-takes-aim-at-previous-govts/articleshow/135849329.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/abandoned-tribals-to-naxal-violence-pm-modi-takes-aim-at-previous-govts/articleshow/135849329.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-15T12:19:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135849505,imgsize-78798.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[IndiGo flight’s landing gear fails to retract after take-off, makes safe emergency 